vents":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4138849991","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/39468#issuecomment-4138849991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/39468","id":4138849991,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY872sdbH","user":{"login":"yurukusa","id":254115176,"node_id":"U_kgDODyV9aA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254115176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa","html_url":"https://github.com/yurukusa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yurukusa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T22:56:28Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T22:56:28Z","body":"Your debug log analysis nails it — the matcher pool count staying constant at 6 confirms that frontmatter-defined hooks are never registered into the active hook resolver.\n**Current workaround**: As you've already found, `hooks/hooks.json` is the reliable path. For scoping the hook to only fire when a specific skill is active, you can add a condition in your script that checks the conversation context:\n```json\n// hooks/hooks.json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Edit\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'input=$(cat); file=$(echo \\\"$input\\\" | jq -r \\\".tool_input.file_path // empty\\\"); if [[ \\\"$file\\\" == *azuredeployparameters.json ]]; then echo \\\"$input\\\" | node hooks/scripts/validate-azdp.js; else exit 0; fi'\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\nThis achieves the same file-scoped validation as the frontmatter approach — the hook fires on all Edit calls but the script only runs validation when the target file matches. Exit code 2 blocks the edit on validation failure.\nThe trade-off vs. frontmatter hooks (when they work) is that `hooks.json` hooks are always active rather than lifecycle-scoped to the skill. But given frontmatter hooks aren't firing at all currently, this is the pragmatic path.\nOne note: this appears to affect both skills and agents frontmatter, so it's likely a single code path where frontmatter hook definitions aren't being merged into the hook matcher registry.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4138849991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4244866039","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/39468#issuecomment-4244866039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/39468","id":4244866039,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY879A4P3",